[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 1. When Aya walks at a speed of \( s \) km/h, the walk takes her 4 hours, including \( t \) minutes spent in the coffee shop. The time spent walking is \( 4 - \frac{t}{60} \) hours. Since the distance is 9 km, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m \[ 9 = s \left( 4 - \frac{t}{60} \right) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 2. When Aya walks at a speed of \( s + 2 \) km/h, the walk takes her 2 hours and 24 minutes (which is 2.4 hours), including \( t \) minutes spent in the coffee shop. The time spent walking is \( 2.4 - \frac{t}{60} \) hours. Since the distance is 9 km, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m \[ 9 = (s + 2) \left( 2.4 - \frac{t}{60} \right) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m We can solve these two equations to find the values of \( s \) and \( t \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2727803)[0m 
